{
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.BeforeYouCanReact": "[pg]Before you can run or react, you feel the unmistakable sensation of being hit with magic. You tremble as you feel drained and fatigued, your spirit and body withering and rotting!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.LikeToTryAgain": "[pg]Would you like to try again?"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.LinesDelineatingGate": "[pg]The lines delineating the gate glow, and before your eyes, the massive obsidian slab of stone disappears, revealing the entrance!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.MagicCircleLightsRunes": "[pg]The magic circle lights up, runes rotating along its center axis. Suddenly, a bright flash emerges from it, leaving you blinded!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.MinusFiveStats": "<b> (-5 to all combat stats!)</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.NotWelcomePay": "[pg][say: You are not welcome here. Pay for your ignorance, and fuel apotheosis.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.WhateverInsideProbablyNot": "[pg]Whatever is inside will probably not be happy about your intrusion. It is best to be prepared. <b>You may not be able to immediately return to your camp afterwards.</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.WordsDisappearAgain": "The words disappear, and soon after a new sentence is written on the gate. [say: Welcome, Wizard. May apotheosis reach us all soon.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AnswerPuzzle.WordsDisappearSoonAfter": "The words disappear, and soon after a new sentence is written on the gate."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AfterSeveralYearsHere": "[pg][say: I understand. After several years here... Vilkus changed. Perhaps living near so much lethicite eventually corrupted his soul and corroded his sanity. Or perhaps his faith finally met its match, and he despaired over the silence of dear old Marae. Regardless, it was high time for him to rest.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ArchInquisitorVilkus": "[pg][say: Vilkus was Arch Inquisitor, the highest rank awarded to any of us. We all followed him, no matter how dire the situation, or how hopeless our prospects. He was the prime example of what an Inquisitor should be, and how the Demon threat should be fought.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskAboutHisPast": "You ask him about his past as a \"person that did a thing\". He contorts for a few moments, visibly uncomfortable with his current position, before answering."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskAboutLockedDoor": "You ask him about the locked door in the nearby corridor."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskAboutSentinels": "[pg]You ask him about the sentinels, and himself."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskAboutTalisman": "You ask him about the talisman you found in Vilkus' body."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskAboutTheExtra": "You ask him about the extra-dimensional maze he banished you to."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskAboutTheHeraldry": "You ask him about the heraldry on his body, or what's been carved of it. It's the same heraldry you found in Inquisitor clothing."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskIfHeHas": "[pg]You ask him if he has a key, or knows what a key might be."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskIfHeKnows": "You ask him if he knows how to leave the tower."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskIfTheres": "[pg]You ask him if there's anything you could do with it."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskWhatHeIs": "[pg]You ask him what he's working on."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskWhoBuiltTower": "You ask him if he knows who built the Tower, or what its purpose is."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskWhoMadeThese": "You ask him who made these living and unliving statues."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskWhoVilkusIs": "You ask him who Vilkus is supposed to be. He shifts a bit, evidently uncomfortable about the topic."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AskWhyHeTurned": "[pg]You ask him why he turned himself into a statue, and not a complete one."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.AttemptsToStrokeIts": "[pg][say: Really?] The statue attempts to stroke its stony beard. [say: Now that is interesting. Since I screwed the spell so skillfully, the only remaining possibility is that someone helped you, like a guardian angel. Or someone that has fun watching you stumble around places. It is probably pretty funny!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.BestWayToAgree": "[pg][say: Ah, shrugging, the best way to agree with someone. Very well, I'll use some of my magic to break the spell sealing the entrance. Just be careful and don't let volcanic dust in the tower. It makes it quite dirty indeed.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ChiefArchitect": "[pg][say: Well. I did. I am, or was, Chief Architect for the Inquisition. I built many things. Armor, weapons, jewelry, and I had the knowledge to transfer someone's essence into an inanimate object, to imbue it with life and hold it under my command.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ClumsilyTurnsToFace": "[pg][say: Oh?] The statue clumsily turns to face his own chest as best he can. [say: Inquisitor... that brings me memories.][pg]He raises his stony brow.[pg][say: Oh! Hoho, nope, gone. How interesting.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ConvincedHeToldYou": "[pg]He smiles, convinced he told you everything you need to know. Not even close to the truth, but it's hard to get anything out of him."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.DidThingInPast": "[pg][say: Well, yes. I do remember that I did a thing in the past. It was very important for the fate of the world, and I was very important too. I can't remember it right now, though. I can't remember much aside from the fact I have to guard Vilkus so he can continue with his work.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.DontLikeToBrag": "[pg][say: Heheh, I don't like to brag, but I did. A bit of magic on a weak target, then poof, marble! Or maybe I make the statue and then use magic to transfer its soul. Or maybe it's none of these things. Who knows, really?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.FocusOnThePurpose": "[pg][say: Yes, yes, focus. As for the Tower's purpose, I truly cannot say. It doesn't seem to be a regular wizard's tower. Those usually have all kinds of amenities, libraries, kitchens, sex dungeons and the like. Ooh, how sinful. The magic runes probably mean something, but I have no idea. My final guess: This tower was built because it could be built. Sometimes that's all the reason you need to do something!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.FromOurScholars": "[pg][say: From what our scholars discovered, Laurentius was an uniquely powerful wizard. He differed from other wizards in his time in that he did not want to return to his home world. He wanted to reshape this one to match his ideals. How megalomaniacal!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.IAmTheKey": "[pg][say: Well, I am the key. I am powering that door's lock with my essence, or soul, or some similar magical nonsense. I could let you inside, but I won't. It's the most FORBIDDEN thing I could imagine! It would be best if you left this matter rest.{0}]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.IWasAnInquisitor": "[pg][say: I was an Inquisitor, back when the order still existed. All who took refuge here were. The Inquisition was a group of warriors and wizards that joined together to fight corruption, no matter the source, and no matter how overwhelming.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.InterestingPushTheIssue": "[pg]Interesting. You push the issue and ask him about the statues' purpose."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.LaurentiusIsTheFirst": "[say: \"Laurentius is the First\". The story of this tower was lost to time, even when civilization wasn't ravaged by the demon menace. I imagine information about it is even harder to find now, since demons are not exactly good at keeping knowledge.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.LittleLeftToDo": "[pg]Well, there's little left to say about it."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.LittlePuzzleOutside": "[pg][say: Well, the little puzzle outside said Laurentius was the First, so I'll assume he built this. I meant to change that puzzle to be harder, but you'd be amazed how hard it is to make a good puzzle. Much harder than solving one, that's for sure!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.LooksLikeNotOpening": "[pg]Looks like you're not opening that door. Not in a friendly manner, anyway."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.MaybeHeBelieved": "[pg][say: Yes, precisely. Maybe he believed I wouldn't serve him eternally if I had full control of myself. I wonder what brought that doubt upon him. Regardless, as time passed I crafted more statues, using whatever prisoners we happened to have captured for interrogation as material. And sometimes I destroyed them, since I saw them as invaders as well. And because it was fun.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.NarrowYourEyes": "[pg]You narrow your eyes."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.NodAndConfirm": "[pg]You nod and confirm."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.NodInUnderstanding": "[pg]You nod in understanding."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.NodQuiteInteresting": "[pg]You nod. Quite interesting."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.NotMuchMaterial": "[pg][say: Oooh, bother. Not a lot of material left to make statues out of, both in marble and souls. Unless you want to help?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.OnlyAQuestion": "[pg][say: Hey, it was only a question.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.PartiallySuccessful": "[pg][say: We were partially successful, but they proved too strong, too numerous to fight back through regular means. We took refuge here. We were ambushed, and here we met our untimely end, most of us turning into the very essence of what we were trying to fight: lethicite.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ProbablyAllYouCan": "[pg]That's probably all you can get out of him."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ProcessIsOneWay": "[pg][say: The process is rather, uhh, one-way. And although it doesn't look like it, the spell did work fully; it's just that, when I attempted it, I really did think this form was good enough for me. So I guess I'll stay here forever. Might rebuild a few of the statues again, order them to unlock the secrets of this tower. It's a hobby, at least.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.QuiteTheAmazingThing": "[pg][say: Quite the amazing thing, isn't it? I wish I could claim ownership of it, but no. That's Laurentius' doing. I merely discovered it and reset the trap, like an unwashed wizard that learns spells from books.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.QuiteTheMystery": "[pg]Quite the mystery. You nod, and think about what he said."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.SaysVisiblyDisappointed": "[pg][say: Oh,] he says, visibly disappointed. [say: That is very sad indeed. Yes, we were all Inquisitors here. Some of us preferred more practical armor, but many wore the heraldry with great pride. Though there isn't much point to it now. Oh well.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ScrapsOfWrittenHistory": "[pg][say: Yes, well, from scraps of written history, it seems he built this tower and lived a solitary life of research and pursue of knowledge. He was quite fond of making golems and living statues--adding life where there was none. I learned much from his writings here, before Vilkus determined we burned all of it to ash. I'm afraid it is all lost now.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ScratchYourHead": "[pg]You scratch your head. This statue truly appears to be addled beyond reason."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.SentinelsOldFriends": "[pg][say: The sentinels outside are... old friends, partners, if you'd like. After the demons ambushed this tower, Vilkus grew increasingly distrustful of the few remaining members of our order, believing that the attack was brought by a betrayer that was still among us. One by one, I turned them into servant statues, at Vilkus' behest.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ShakeHeadTellTomb": "[pg]You shake your head, and tell him that you found the clothes in an old tomb."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ShapeThatTalisman": "[pg][say: You? Nothing. Me? I can shape that talisman into one item of fearsome power! It is supposed to only be given to Inquisitors, but considering the circumstance, I'll let it slide. Now, what are you thinking about?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.SighAskFocus": "[pg]You sigh and ask him to focus on the question."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.SighTellKillVilkus": "[pg]You sigh, and tell him that you had no choice but to kill Vilkus when he attacked you."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.SighsLooksSadFor": "[pg]Jeremiah sighs, and looks sad for the first time since you met him. Best to leave it alone for now."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.SomeAcceptedOpportunity": "[pg][say: Some of them accepted the opportunity to serve the Inquisition with honor. Some others... not so much.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.SpeculateIfItWas": "[pg]You speculate if it was to prevent anyone from disturbing him."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.TellHimAnotherMaze": "[pg]You tell him that another maze materialized beneath yours, one with a clone of yourself and an exit."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ThankHimForThe": "[pg]Shame. You thank him for the information."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ThenAskWhyHe": "[pg]You then ask him why he hasn't finished the job or reversed the spell, now that he has his sanity back."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ThingThatAmazesMe": "[pg][say: *cough* Weeell, the thing that amazes me is that you actually managed to leave it. I was very careful to recklessly destroy as much of the magical matrix surrounding the corridor as possible, to turn a fun puzzle into a nightmare realm of certain death. How did you do that?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ThinkIKnewOnce": "[pg][say: I don't know. I think I knew, once. But that memory is very out of my reach, much like anything more than two feet away from me. I'd tell you to go ask that to him personally, but that is forbidden.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.ThoughtTheseWereLost": "[pg][say: Oooh, interesting. I thought these were lost to time. Those talismans were a token of trust given to honored Inquisitors for feats of strength and faith. They contain great magical potential, and I can't help but wonder why Vilkus did not make use of it. Maybe he didn't feel worthy? Hm, worth a thought.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.VeryWellLocked": "[pg][say: Yes, it is very well locked. What about it?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.VilkusSetsTheRules": "[pg][say: Vilkus is the person that sets the rules. He told me not to allow anyone inside, so his work isn't disturbed. Disturbing his work is very forbidden. I took an oath not to do it, I think.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.WhateverYouWant": "[pg][say: Whatever you want! The three statues outside are set up for defensive purposes, another layer of measures to prevent Vilkus from being bothered. Though if you are here, I'm guessing they're quite destroyed right now.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.WhenInevitableTimeCame": "[pg][say: Hrmph. When the inevitable time came where Vilkus ordered me to turn myself into an eternal sentinel, I accepted the task, both to prove my loyalty and to defend him eternally. However, in the middle of the process, he sabotaged it, and cast a spell to warp my mind, imbuing it with only a few basic directives.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.WorthATry": "[pg]Well, it was worth a try."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.WouldBeHardIndeed": "[pg][say: Yes, I imagine that would be hard indeed, if you are not capable of teleportation. Hmrhgh. Vilkus told me that allowing anyone inside is FORBIDDEN. So I guess that allowing you to leave is the most un-FORBIDDEN thing I could possibly do!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.YouGlareAtHim": "[pg]You glare at him."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.YouRecognizeIt": "[pg][say: You recognize it? Does that mean... does the Inquisition still act in Mareth?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AskQuestion.YouShrug": "[pg]You shrug."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AttackJeremiah.ConstructRaisesItsArm": "[pg]The construct raises its one sculpted arm, and pieces of nearby statues start moving on their own, reassembling themselves!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AttackJeremiah.FightingArchitectJeremiah": "[pg]You're fighting <b>Architect Jeremiah!</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AttackJeremiah.MagicAlwaysUseful": "[pg][say: Magic! Always useful stuff. Well, if you're about to try to destroy me, I suppose it is only fair that I try to destroy you. Alright now!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AttackJeremiah.ReadyYourAndPosition": "You ready your [weapon] and position yourself to destroy the marble statue and open the locked door."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AttackJeremiah.SighAndStrikeStatue": "[pg]You sigh, and strike the statue with all your might. To your surprise, you barely make a dent in the marble!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.AttackJeremiah.WouldntDoThat": "[pg][say: Oh, I wouldn't do that if I were you. But if I were you, I wouldn't be me, so I wouldn't die if you succeeded. So maybe I would!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.ConfirmAcquired.DontMentionIt": "[pg][say: Don't mention it. Seriously, don't mention it. I don't want more demons to ambush this place.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.ConfirmAcquired.TakeYourReward": "You take your reward. Just touching it fills you with power and determination. You thank Jeremiah for the item."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Corridor.CorridorLeadsToMuch": "The corridor leads to a much more open area, opening up on both sides and the ceiling to reveal a massive circular room that absolutely dwarfs you. You cannot see the ceiling when you look skywards. A massive pillar of the same smooth obsidian sits on its center, stretching towards the sky. The light pulses continue to emerge from the corridor, climbing the pillar and alighting several thousand runes along its height."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Corridor.FreedFromTheMaze": "[pg]Now freed from the maze, you're able to proceed."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.GiveHimTheTalisman": "You give him the talisman and tell him you want the Flameheart Spear."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.GiveTalismanRing": "You give him the talisman and tell him you want the Flamespirit Ring."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.GiveTalismanShield": "You give him the talisman and tell him you want the Flamegrit Shield."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.HoldsCircularTalisman": "[pg]Jeremiah holds the circular talisman with its single available hand. It glows as he utters words of power, and before your eyes, it morphs into a beautiful black and gold spear, which appears to gleam and shine even in complete absence of light. It is truly a marvelous weapon, worthy of the most honored of Inquisitors."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.HoldsCircularTalismanAgain": "[pg]Jeremiah holds the circular talisman with its single available hand. It glows as he utters words of power, and before your eyes, it morphs into an exquisite black and gold shield which appears to gleam and shine even in complete absence of light. It is truly a marvelous shield, worthy of the most honored of Inquisitors."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.HoldsCircularTalismanThird": "[pg]Jeremiah holds the circular talisman with its single available hand. It glows as he utters words of power, and before your eyes, it morphs into an exquisite black and gold ring which appears to gleam and shine even in complete absence of light. It is truly a marvelous piece of jewelry, worthy of the most honored of Inquisitors."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.IMissedDoingThat": "[pg][say: I missed doing that, really. Here you go, have fun with it. I'd tell you to only slay demons and corrupted foes, but I'm willing to guess there's not many pure beings left, after all these years.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.MarvelousLetWork": "[pg][say: Marvelous, marvelous. Now, let me work.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.MarvelousLetWorkAgain": "[pg][say: Marvelous, marvelous. Now, let me work.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.MarvelousLetWorkThird": "[pg][say: Marvelous, marvelous. Now, let me work.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.MissedDoingAgain": "[pg][say: I missed doing that, really. Here you go, have fun with it. I'd tell you to only slay demons and corrupted foes, but I'm willing to guess there's not many pure beings left, after all these years.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.CraftWeapon.MissedDoingThird": "[pg][say: I missed doing that, really. Here you go, have fun with it. I'd tell you to only slay demons and corrupted foes, but I'm willing to guess there's not many pure beings left, after all these years.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatJeremiah.FinalStrikeYouFinally": "With a final strike, you finally manage to crack Jeremiah's magical armor, ripping off a chunk of his \"body\"."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatJeremiah.HearFaintRumbling": "[pg]You hear a faint rumbling and crackling sound deep in the nearby corridor. True to his insane word, the door that leads further ahead is now open."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatJeremiah.StrikeStatueAgain": "[pg]You strike the statue again before it can talk any more, shattering it into a hundred pieces. He is silenced, finally."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatJeremiah.WhatDyingIsLike": "[pg][say: So this is what it's like, dying. I would document this, but I don't think I'll have time.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.AbstractLandscapeAround": "[pg]Gradually, the abstract landscape around you reforms, and you find yourself at the top of the tower again. Laurentius stands at its center, facing you."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.BodyDiesSoulEndures": "[pg][say: Remember, [name]. The body can die. Your soul Endures forever.] "
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.BringingMeHope": "[pg][say: Thank you, [name]. For bringing me hope, for Mareth and all living things. There may one day come a time where this world withers and dies. In that day, I hope you are here, to rekindle its soul as you have done mine, and reshape it, to save it from the mistakes of the past.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.CareNotMattersNot": "[pg][say: I care not, and it matters not. All that is can be known. I did not challenge you to test your knowledge. I challenged you to see your willingness to learn.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.HitWizardAndFor": "You hit the wizard, and, for the first time, he recoils and falls, feeling genuine pain."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.MoveForwardEager": "[pg]You move forward, eager to finish this duel on your favor. Before you can strike, however, he disappears."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.NewAbilitySoulburst": "[pg]<b>New ability acquired: Soulburst!</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.SmilePantingExhaustion": "[pg]You smile, panting with exhaustion. His face becomes serious. He turns, to face the Volcanic Crag."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.SuddenlyItVanishes": "Suddenly, it vanishes, along with the old wizard.[pg]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.TapsStaffOnThe": "[pg]Laurentius taps his staff on the floor. An enormous beam of light strikes from the skies, enveloping him."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.TellReallyDontKnow": "[pg]You tell him you really don't know how to save Mareth. Not in that way."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatLaurentius.YouGaveMePause": "[pg][say: Exquisite! Truly exquisite. I have battled many foes in my time, [name], but you... you gave me pause. Someone of your skill has true potential, and I can only hope that one day you fully control it.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.ApproachCorruptedInquisitor": "[pg]You approach the corrupted Inquisitor, ready to deliver the final blow."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.AreYouAbandoningMe": "[pg][say: Marae... are you abandoning me? Are we not worthy? So many of us gone, so much of this land defiled... and it isn't enough? Why... Why?!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.BringsHandToHis": "[pg]He brings his hand to his chest, casting his final spell on himself. He immediately bursts into flames, screaming loudly, and in a short few moments he's completely scorched and charred."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.FaithDiedToo": "[pg][say: And now... Faith has died as well.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.FinallyRelax": "[pg]You finally relax as you see his body turning to ash. Although he was a fierce opponent, you can't help but feel a tinge of melancholy over his fate."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.KeyItemTalismanOf": "[pg]Key Item acquired: <b>Talisman of the Flame!</b>[pg]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.LiftsHandAndPrepares": "[pg]He lifts a hand and prepares a spell of whitefire. He still has some fight left in him!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.OneObjectSurvives": "[pg]One object survives the Inquisitor's self-immolation: A small circular emblem of an everlasting fire. You pick it up, wondering if it has any use."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.VilkusFallsTrembling": "Vilkus falls, trembling and bleeding."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatVilkus.WeAreDoomed": "[pg][say: We are all doomed, then. When the demons ambushed us, hope finally died. And now...]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedByJeremiah.CastsSpellOnYou": "[pg]He casts the spell on you, and you black out."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedByJeremiah.CastsTheSpellAgain": "[pg]He casts the spell on you, and you black out."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedByJeremiah.FallOverwhelmedByDesire": "You fall, overwhelmed by desire."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedByJeremiah.FallOverwhelmedInjuries": "You fall, overwhelmed by your injuries."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedByJeremiah.TryGetUp": "[pg][say: By Marae, teased to submission by a marble statue. Can't blame you, though. I know I would try to do <b>that</b>, if I were ambulatory.][pg]You attempt to get up and strike the talkative statue again, but the succubus statue holds you, and begins fondling your body sensually. You moan, and your mind loses all offensive intent.[pg][say: Well, despite your sinful ways, I do think you were quite competent to make it this far. I think Vilkus would approve if I added another layer of defenses against any future invaders.][pg]With his single free arm, he begins weaving some type of spell. The succubus's care prevents you from focusing on the threat for long, though; you're soon hypnotized by her movement again.[pg][say: Don't worry, being marble is not so bad! Well, I would say that, of course, but it is true.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedByJeremiah.TryGetUpAgain": "[pg][say: Golems can be quite dangerous, can't they? Unthinking, unfeeling, powerful magic making them almost invincible. Yeesh, wouldn't want to be on your spot right now!][pg]You attempt to get up and strike the talkative statue again, but the incubus statue delivers a swift kick to your stomach, leaving you breathless.[pg][say: Well, despite your sinful ways, I do think you were quite competent to make it this far. I think Vilkus would approve if I added another layer of defenses against any future invaders.][pg]With his single free arm, he begins weaving some type of spell. The incubus holds you down, and prevents you from getting up.[pg][say: Don't worry, being marble is not so bad! Well, I would say that, of course, but it is true.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedBySentinels.FallOverwhelmedByEnemies": "You fall, overwhelmed by your enemies. The Warrior and the Naked Man approach you to confirm their victory, while the Wizard kneels in a prayer. You stare at them, their marble eyes piercing you and filling you with fear for your fate."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedBySentinels.OneLastTwitchAttempt": "[pg]With one last twitch, you attempt a half-hearted attack, which sends the Naked Man running back in horror. The Warrior stands still, and your attack bounces harmlessly on the enchanted stone. He raises his spear and points it down, towards your heart. You cringe, preparing for the upcoming attack."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedBySentinels.PlungesWeaponDown": "[pg]He plunges his weapon down, easily piercing through your [armor] and skin, wounding your heart. You feel pain, the taste of blood, and then cold. Absolute cold."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedBySentinels.VictoryConfirmedWarrior": "[pg]His victory confirmed, the Warrior returns to the other two statues, and they soon revert to their previous, immortal scene."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedByVilkus.FallIncapableOfCombat": "You fall, incapable of continuing combat."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DefeatedByVilkus.TwirlsHisEstoc": "[pg][say: Marae, I do not doubt your wisdom. I have proven my faith time and again. I will stay here, protecting my fallen comrades, awaiting your blessing, your revelation.][pg]He twirls his estoc and moves towards you.[pg][say: And whenever demons find their way into this sanctuary...][pg]He plunges his estoc into your chest, making you cough blood and groan.[pg][say: They shall be purged, as the Inquisition once did.][pg]He twists the blade, destroying your heart, and swiftly erasing your life.[pg][say: Merciful Marae, thank you for this chance to prove myself again.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.DimensionalShift2.AlmostAsSuddenly": "Almost as suddenly as it started, it ends, and you find yourself in a sufficiently well lit room. Breathing rapidly, you get up and begin analyzing your surroundings."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.BrandishesHisEstoc": "[pg]He brandishes his estoc as best he can. [say: So many years waiting, and Marae gives me one final test of my resolve. Very well. In this day, the Inquisition purges anew.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.CacklesAndCoughs": "[pg]He cackles and coughs. [say: That so? Such lies are most sinful, wretched creature. You will pay doubly for those.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.CenterOfRoom": "[pg]At the center of the room is a cloaked, masked figure in tattered red robes, sitting in an old wooden ornate chair and weakly holding an estoc."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.CloakedFigureGetsUp": "[pg][say: So... Jeremiah has betrayed me. Or maybe you destroyed him. Either way, that proves the weakness of his faith.] The cloaked figure gets up from his chair, trembling, using his estoc for support. The tattered robe reveals a bit of his skin. Old, scarred, thin and weathered."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.FaintlyPulsesWithEnergy": "[pg]He faintly pulses with energy, and points his estoc at you.<b>You are fighting Arch Inquisitor Vilkus!</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.MoveUpStairsSlowly": "You move up the stairs, slowly and carefully. The darkness that covered your ascension is overtaken by a dim light as you reach a massive, domed chamber. The top of the dome has a hole through which ambient light pours, lighting particles of dust and a strange fog that lingers perpetually on the floor."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.OldManNotDemon": "[pg]You tell the old man that you are no demon{0}."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.SixteenLethiciteCrystals": "[pg]Sixteen lethicite crystals of varying sizes adorn gothic pedestals placed in alcoves along the edge of the chamber. They pulse, brimming with unholy power."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EncounterVilkus.WillNotLetTake": "[pg][say: I will not let you take them, demon! Marae guides me, and she will reveal me the way soon. I know... I have Faith.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EndPuzzle.AfterAMoment": "[pg]After a moment, it too is launched into space. You begin falling into the ether, but before you can scream, the uncomfortable and indescribable feeling of being folded into yourself strikes you again."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EndPuzzle.AnalyzeEnvironment": "You analyze your environment, the circumstances surrounding it. Your clone, the maze, the infinity of space. This is an illusion. It has to be! You close your eyes and focus, using your magic to break through whatever spell is currently afflicting you."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EndPuzzle.BlinkOutOfExistence": "[pg]You blink out of existence."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EndPuzzle.LikeAPersonStuck": "[pg]Like a person stuck in a lucid dream, you attempt to return to your real self. The spell proves resilient, but using your superior intellect, you slowly perceive reality again. The coldness of the corridor. The pulses of light. The humming runes. The old voice. One by one, your senses help you break the illusion forced upon you. You then open your eyes, and blink out of existence."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EndPuzzle.MirrorSelfReachesIts": "As your mirror-self reaches its exit, the mazes begins to disappear. One by one, pieces of the walls, ceiling and floor dash out onto infinity in absurd speeds. Soon, the only piece remaining is the one under your feet."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterDungeon.AfterFewDifficultMinutes": "[pg]After a few difficult minutes, you're at the base of the cliff, and the sheer scale of the tower becomes more apparent to you. It is one of the most impressive things you've seen in Mareth yet, even in its decrepit state. You continue your approach."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterDungeon.ArduousTravelsVolcanic": "Your arduous travels along the Volcanic Crag finally bear fruit. You reach the top of a cliff, and are amazed by what you see; On the horizon, in the middle of a cracked and scorched plain, lies a massive, half-toppled tower."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterDungeon.CloserFireWind": "[pg]As you get closer, the fire-hot wind becomes stronger, lifting volcanic ash in great waves that makes it difficult to both see and breathe. Unbidden, you narrow your eyes and soldier on."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterDungeon.MoveAheadHikingDown": "[pg]You move ahead, carefully hiking down the jagged cliff. Traveling through the Crag is always a complex task, but the rocks are especially treacherous here, the hill obscenely steep."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterDungeon.SixHundredFeetTall": "[pg]It is easily 600 feet tall. Its obsidian surface gleams even in the scarce light that manages to pierce the volcanic dust and ash that clouds the area. Along its trapezoidal length, several cracks and missing pieces scar the otherwise mirror-polished surface of the tower. You notice a massive embossed circle at its top, though you can't make out details from the distance you're at."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterDungeonpt2.EnterTheTower": "[pg]Do you enter the tower or leave?"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterDungeonpt2.StandingBeforeGate": "[pg]Standing in front of the gate are three stone statues. One depicts a warrior, armored in exquisite plate armor, wielding a spear. The second depicts a wizard, clad in robes, holding a book in one hand, staff in another. The third, is of a naked man, wielding a shield. They show a curious scene; the Warrior points his spear at the naked man, his gaze clearly one of rage and anger. The Wizard holds her staff aloft, towards the sky, eyes closed and book held tightly against her chest. The Naked Man cowers, protecting himself with his shield while standing in a fetal position.[pg]The statues are cracked and covered with volcanic ash. It stands curiously distinct from the rest of the landscape. You're unsure what it is supposed to represent."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterDungeonpt2.TowerOfDeceptionIs": "[pg]<b>The Tower of Deception is now accessible from the 'Dungeons' submenu inside 'Places' menu.</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterForReal.FightOnYourHands": "[pg]You have a fight on your hands!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterForReal.MoveTowardsGateIgnoring": "You move towards the gate, ignoring the statues."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterForReal.StandAtGate": "You stand at the gate of the obsidian Tower. The statues are destroyed and inert, barely visible now that the dust storms have buried them. The uncomfortable heat and tearing wind force you to make a decision: Will you enter the mysterious tower or leave?"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterForReal.TouchTheSmoothSurface": "[pg]When you touch the smooth surface of the gate, you hear rumbling and the sound of stone rubbing against stone behind you, even through the howling of the volcanic dust storms."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterForReal.TurnAroundAndBehold": "[pg]You turn around and behold the three statues once again. They have shifted from their still scene, and are now all staring at you, their emotionless gaze sending you warnings of danger."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterForReal.WarriorIsTheFirst": "[pg]The Warrior is the first one to move again, pointing its spear defiantly at you. The Wizard follows by brandishing her staff, and the Naked Man weakly raises his shield."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterTowerDimensionalShift.AfterMinutesOfWalking": "[pg]After minutes of walking, all you see is pitch black. The corridor is unnaturally long; you're sure you have walked the width of the tower by now. You turn around, but there's not even a glint of the exterior's light. Your stomach sinks as you realize you may have been lured into a trap."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterTowerDimensionalShift.InAFlashCorridor": "[pg]In a flash, the entire corridor lights up, and you're thrown to the ground by an unseen force. You get up, dazed, feeling as if you're being pushed to every direction at once, the corridor spinning and rotating, falling and being raised. You nearly hurl on the spot as the corridor itself stretches, widening, heightening and shortening in random amounts. You look at your hands and panic as they too begin morphing, bending in impossible dimensions!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterTowerDimensionalShift.PulseOfLightIrradiates": "[pg]Suddenly, a pulse of light irradiates from the floor beneath you, several glowing lines dashing from your position and moving towards the darkness, crawling between the divisions of the mirror-polished obsidian slabs. The light converges into one point in the distance, almost too far to see."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.EnterTowerDimensionalShift.StepInsideObsidianTower": "You step inside the obsidian tower, moving into a pitch black corridor, weapons at the ready for any ambush. The sweltering heat of the landscape behind you is soon replaced by a rather noticeable coolness. You move forward slowly, stepping ever more carefully as the natural light from the exterior dims."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.ExitDungeon.TurnBackOnTower": "You turn your back on the Tower and head back to camp."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.FinalDoor.DistinctSenseOf": " There is a distinct sense of foreboding as you look to the darkness above. <b>You should be ready for a long, grueling fight.</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.FinalDoor.JeremiahsSealUndone": "With Jeremiah's seal undone, the door that once blocked this corridor is now unlocked, though it is still hard to push open due to its sheer heft."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.FinalDoor.SilenceDeafening": "[pg]The silence here is deafening, and you can no longer hear the humming of the magical pulses that exist in the rest of the Tower."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.FinalDoor.ThisSectionOfTower": "[pg]While this section of the tower was silent before, it now hums and pulses with light, much like the rest of the building. The pulses of light move upstairs, beckoning you to visit Vilkus' grave once again."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.FinalDoor.ToTheNorthAnother": "[pg]To the north, there's another set of stairs, similar in length to the one that led you to the study room."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LaurentiusChallenge.WouldYouFaceMe": "[say: You would face me? I wonder, do you do this out of courage, or foolishness? It matters not, I suppose. Still, I ask you this final time. Do you really want to face me?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LaurentiusChallenge2.FightingAnAspect": "[pg]<b>You are fighting an Aspect of Laurentius!</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LaurentiusChallenge2.HopedYoudSayThat": "[pg][say: Yes, I had hoped you'd say that. Very well then, Champion, test your might against me, so that the forge of your soul can burn like the sun itself!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LaurentiusChallenge2.RisesUpGlowing": "[pg]The wizard rises up, glowing, and fiercely waves his staff once, beckoning you to fight. You ready your [weapon] and prepare yourself!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LaurentiusChallenge2.ShowMeYourWill": "[pg][say: Show me the strength of your will, Champion! Show me that you are worthy of holding Reality upon your shoulders!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LaurentiusChallenge2.TapsStaffAgainst": "[pg]The wizard taps his staff against the floor, and the area around the top of the Tower is enveloped in energy. With another tap, your surroundings crack like glass, throwing the two of you into cosmic infinity!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LaurentiusChallenge2.TellThatYouDo": "You tell him that you do indeed want to challenge him. He opens up a smile."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LeaveLaurentius.AskIfHeKnows": "You ask him if he knows of a way to bring you back down, somehow."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LeaveLaurentius.CanDoThatInvite": "[pg][say: Yes, [name]. I can do that. My invite remains, however. If you feel that the forge of your soul is strong enough... return here. You know the way.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LeaveLaurentius.LaurentiusCanBeEncountered": "[pg]<b>Laurentius can now be encountered in the Camp Actions menu.</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LeaveLaurentius.WaveOfHisHand": "With a wave of his hand, you are enveloped in a glowing blue barrier. You levitate. With another wave, you disappear."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LoseToLaurentius.FallIncapableContinuing": "You fall, incapable of continuing your duel. Laurentius stops levitating, and slowly walks towards you."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LoseToLaurentius.FireThatTempers": "[pg][say: Return here when you desire to try again. Remember, [name], it is the fire that tempers the blade. I do not expect you to succeed without pain.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LoseToLaurentius.NodPantingExhaustion": "[pg]You nod, panting with exhaustion."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LoseToLaurentius.NotReadyYet": "[pg][say: You are not ready yet. That is fine. I will stay here, and wait for you to refine yourself.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LoseToLaurentius.TouchOfStaff": "[pg]With a touch of his staff, you feel energized enough to stand. He taps his staff against the abstract floor, and the two of you are returned to the top of the Tower."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.LoseToLaurentius.TurnsToFaceVolcanic": "[pg]He turns to face the Volcanic Crag. With a wave of his hand, a massive beam of light surges from the sky, lifting you from the ground. Soon, you disappear."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.AfterInitialRecoil": "[pg]After your initial recoil, you turn your head slightly and answer that yes, you are real."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.ApproachHalfSculpted": "You approach the half-sculpted Inquisitor. It immediately turns its face towards you, with the usual gaze of someone who is lost, but happy."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.AskQuestionAgain": "[pg]You ask your question again."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.CarefullyApproachStatue": "You carefully approach the statue, wary of any more extra-dimensional traps."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.ConfrontHimWithInfo": "[pg]You confront him with that information."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.IDidMazeYou": "[pg][say: I did Maze you, didn't I? Did I? I don't know, really. My memory isn't very good nowadays... when I begin remembering stuff, it just clears up again!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.InefficacyWasWith": "[pg][say: Or I guess, in this case, the inefficacy was witnessed by my eyes. Good to see you're alive, though. If you are alive. Vilkus didn't tell me to kill anything that left the maze, so I guess I won't. IIII'm Jeremiah, person that did a thing in the past. Nice to meet you.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.MoveBackToAnalyze": "[pg]You move back to analyze the whole sculpture. Well crafted, but nothing necessarily unique about it."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.OhHohoSorry": "[pg][say: Oh, hoho, sorry. Well, if I mazed you, then that's because you are an invader. That is one of my jobs, you know. Send anything that enters this tower to that extradimensional maze, so they won't bother Vilkus. Hah, curious is the trap maker's art, isn't it? Its efficacy unwitnessed by its own eyes.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.PersonMetBefore": "[pg][say: Heeey, person I have met before. Good to see you again.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.RaiseABrow": "[pg]You raise a brow."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.SeenItBefore": " You've seen it before; it's the Inquisitor heraldry!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.SomethingInThatVoice": "[pg]Something in that voice is familiar. You ponder it for a few moments and it becomes clear; this is the same voice you heard when you were sent to the maze!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.StatueSmilesAtYou": "[pg]The statue smiles at you. It appears genuinely unaware of how dire your situation was just minutes ago. You tell him your name and think about what to do next."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.UntilItTurnsIts": "[pg]That is, until it turns its head and starts speaking."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.WellHelloThere": "[pg][say: Well, hello there. You seem to be pretty interested in me! That's fine, I'm interested in you too, hehe- erh, not in the way you'd expect. You're real, aren't you?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.WhatHallucinationWouldSay": "[pg][say: That is exactly what a hallucination would say! Or maybe the hallucinations want me to think that they would say that, so that I wouldn't pay attention to real people. Well, I'll just have to go with Faith here. IIIIt's what we do.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetJeremiah.WhatHasBeenSculpted": "[pg]What has been sculpted out of the marble is exquisite; the old man's face and beard are crafted to perfection. His upper body is clad in beautiful hooded robes, and the sword heraldry emblazoned within is elegant, too."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius.GlowingPulsesGrow": "[pg]The glowing pulses grow in strength once you're at the center. Before you can react, you're lifted by an unknown force. You struggle, but merely shift on your own axis, completely devoid of gravity. The humming and radiance of the pulses become deafening."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius.IntoPillarOfLight": "You walk into the pillar of light. Your body tingles and faintly vibrates as you're covered in the magical luminosity, and you're soon blinded by the radiance."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius.OneFinalPulseStrikes": "[pg]One final pulse strikes, and you vanish, along with the pillar of light."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius2.CenterOfArea": "[pg]At the center of the area stands a tall, middle aged man with shoulder length, auburn hair. He is wearing black and gold robes and carrying an ornate steel staff, with a bright red gem in its top. He has his back turned to you, one fist clutched behind it."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius2.ComeToAmazed": "You come to, amazed at your recent extra-corporeal experience, but not harmed in any way."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius2.LookAroundSomehowEnded": "[pg]You look around. Somehow, you ended up at the top of the Tower! It is flat, made of material similar to the rest of the structure. Runes adorn two concentric circles carved into the stone, and they somehow turn and spin through their length, as if floating on a thin sheet of water."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius2.MassiveStormsAndGusts": "[pg]The massive storms and gusts of volcanic ash rage harder at this altitude, but, somehow, you are not affected by them in the slightest. Must be some type of protective field."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.AWonderIsntIt": "[pg][say: A wonder, isn't it? This tower, I mean. I see you're cautious. Don't worry. I mean you no harm.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.AllWorldsChange": "[pg][say: I have, as a matter of fact. [name], all worlds change. They all grow, wither and die, as mortal as any living thing within it. Mareth is proof that even the Gods, to which we all look towards, can fail, fall, and disappear. The reason I'm here... Mareth is dying, [name].]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.ApproachMysteriousWizard": "You approach the mysterious wizard. He nods and greets you."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.ApproachRobedFigure": "You approach the robed figure, with the usual caution that this place requires."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.AskIfHeIntends": "[pg]You ask him if he intends to reinvent the world. He smiles."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.AskIfSuchThing": "[pg]You ask if such a thing is even possible for mortals, no matter how powerful."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.BreakSilenceAndAsk": "[pg]You break your silence, and ask what he's doing here, and who he is. He breathes deeply, thinking."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.BringsHandTo": "[pg][say: Perhaps they were afraid of themselves, the power they wielded. Perhaps the only way they found to unleash their full potential was to destroy whatever brought them conscience]--the man brings a hand to his chest and holds a small necklace, a lethicite crystal encrusted within--[say: so they could see how deeply their influence could alter the fabric of reality.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.BroughtPeaceToVilkus": "[pg][say: You were the one that brought peace to Vilkus. I thank you for that. Mareth changed too much for a man like him. Even if he somehow managed to find a way to save his fellow Inquisitors, he would soon discover that the world he inhabited was not the same he left, not the same he suffered so much for.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.FindTheOneCan": "[pg][say: My plan is to find the one that can, and challenge him for the right of Divinity.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.IfHeHoldsAny": "[pg][say: Not mine, no. I have attempted it, and found myself lacking,] he says. If he holds any anger or disappointment over his failure, he does a perfect job of hiding it."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.LastWordGrabsAttention": "[pg]That last word grabs your attention. You look at the blasted landscape of the crag, and ask him exactly what he means by that."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.MomentToParse": "[pg]You take a moment to parse his words, and ask him if his goal is to become a wizard of such power, then."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.MuchLikeLovedGrandfather": "[pg][say: Much like a loved grandfather, affected by a bout of grievous pestilence. We can attempt a cure with tremendous effort, but time moves ever forward, and its end is known to us all. If we want to make him immortal, we must preserve its legacy, not its being.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.NeverHadAnyConscience": "[pg][say: Or perhaps they never had any conscience at all, and they merely wanted to confirm it.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.NodButPointOut": "[pg]You nod, but point out that he hasn't answered your question."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.PausesForASecond": "[pg]He pauses for a second, and looks upwards."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.PurposeWorthyOfThe": "[pg][say: Perhaps not. But that is a purpose worthy of the mightiest wizard. Something to focus on, so it is not led astray. We do not know our true limits, and I believe that for such a noble purpose, we are righteous in attempting to surpass them.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.ReasonIAmHere": "[pg][say: Yes. The reason why I am here. Why this Tower is here. To see if this world can be forged anew, its legacy preserved, the mistakes of the past mere memories, so they are not repeated.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.SighsABitMelancholy": "[pg]He sighs, a bit melancholy."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.StareInSilence": "[pg]You stare at him in silence, and nod briefly. He laughs."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.VoiceYourAgreement": "[pg]You voice your agreement as you drop your guard and approach him. He looks at you with kindness, and smiles as you face him."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MeetLaurentius3.WizardsOfOld": "[pg][say: Wizards of old, they had great power. More than they could wield, more than they had any purpose for. They were all children, playing with fire, the first in their line to tap into the true potential of mortal creatures. The first to challenge the Old Gods themselves.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle.CorridorLeadsToMuch": "[pg]The corridor leads to a much more open area, opening up on both sides and the ceiling to reveal a massive circular room that absolutely dwarfs you. You cannot see the ceiling when you look skywards. A massive pillar of the same smooth obsidian sits on its center, stretching towards the sky. The light pulses continue to emerge from the corridor, climbing the pillar and alighting several thousand runes along its height."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle.MoveAwayFromCorpses": "You move away from the corpses and step forward towards the unknown."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle.TakeAStep": "[pg]You take a step in this massive room. You do not move forward, however."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle.TakeAnotherStep": "[pg]You take another step, and you find yourself four steps back. You start running, and with each step, you move backwards, sidewards, up and down. You stop, breathless, and notice you haven't actually moved a single inch."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.AnInvaderAfterYears": "[pg][say: An invader? After all these years? This is bothersome indeed.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.BlinkOfAnEye": "[pg]In the blink of an eye, you disappear, your body folding in on itself and popping out of existence."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.ForgotWhatImSupposed": "[pg][say: I forgot what I'm supposed to do now... Ah yes! The Mazing. It was nice to know you, eer- whoever you are, invader.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.LookAroundAttempting": "[pg]You look around, attempting to find the source, with no success."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.MarvelousTraps": "[pg][say: Marvelous traps. Laurentius knew what he was doing! The only bad part is that he added an exit. But, well, I fixed that!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.OldTremblingVoice": "An old, trembling high-pitched voice echoes through the room."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.TakeAnotherStepForward": "[pg]You take another step forward, but the Tower's magic continues to elude your attempts."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.WeStillHaveTime": "[pg][say: Well, no matter. We still have time, yes. There is always more time.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle2.WhateverThatIsCant": "[pg]Whatever that is, it can't be good. You begin a sprint back towards the corridor, but despite your efforts, you're still unable to actually change your position. You then notice the floor distancing from your feet, the walls disappearing into the distance."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle3.BriefAnalysisNotice": "[pg]From a brief analysis, you notice that the configuration of your clone's maze is different from yours, and in one way in particular: it contains an exit! <b>You'll have to figure out a way to lead your clone to its exit. Maybe you'll also be freed then?</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle3.ComeToCompletely": "You come to in a completely different place, screaming. You examine your surroundings and notice you're in some kind of glass maze. You look up and down and your stomach sinks as you realize the room is apparently floating in space itself. Stars dot every single direction you look at, and there doesn't seem to be any way to break free."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle3.CrouchForBetter": "[pg]You crouch to get a better look at the poor devil, and another vision bends your mind; that person is yourself... also crouched and looking downwards! You get up in surprise, and your other self does the same. You move forward, and it does too."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.MirrorPuzzle3.SomethingMorphs": "[pg]Suddenly, something morphs into existence under the glass maze, unfolding itself in a manner inverse to what happened to you. As it stretches outwards from itself, you realize it is another glass maze, it too containing a prisoner."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.NotAcquired.AbsolutelyNot": "[pg]Absolutely not."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.NotAcquired.CantMakeEffort": "[pg][say: Can't you make an effort?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.NotAcquired.ReturnWhenAble": "[pg][say: Very well. Return when you're able to actually get it, then.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.NotAcquired.TellJeremiahYoureNot": "You tell Jeremiah you're not really capable of carrying the item right now."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Pillar.GoingAroundPillar": "Going around the massive pillar just makes more evident that this tower does not conform to regular conventions of space. It was sizable on the outside, but the scale of your surroundings and the pillar defies ordinary expectation. This is a marvel of engineering, magical or otherwise."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Pillar2.AheadLiesSteepStaircase": "[pg]Ahead lies a massive, steep staircase, that winds towards a higher level at the back of the colossal pillar."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Pillar2.PosesVarySome": "[pg]Their poses vary; some of them are cowering in horror, others are laughing, others apparently are in the middle of climax with other demons. The craftsmanship is superb, and the marble truly looks like flesh, each muscle and tendon sculpted to a level of skill you didn't imagine possible."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Pillar2.SawPlentyOfCorpses": "While you saw plenty of corpses in the corridor, what you see here is less gruesome, reminding you instead of the sentinels guarding the entrance to the tower. Several statues--and statue pieces--are littered throughout the area. They all depict demons: incubi, succubi, omnibi and imps."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Redraw.CloneReachesItsExit": "Your clone reaches its exit."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Redraw.FontB": "</font></b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Redraw.FontFaceTypewriter": "<b><font face=\"_typewriter\">"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RoomEntrance.StandingInExtremely": "You're standing in an extremely spacious corridor, made completely out of some sort of obsidian stone, polished to a mirror shine. Magical runes adorn much of the walls and ceiling. Every once in a while, a pulse of light crawls through the corridor with an audible hum, like a high pitched glass harp, causing the runes to glow intensely for a few moments."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RoomEntrance2.CursoryExamination": "[pg]From a cursory examination, you'd wager these bodies are a decade old, maybe more."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RoomEntrance2.DespiteSourcelessLight": "Despite the sourceless light that allows you to move forward, this section of the corridor still puts you on edge. Blood and scorch marks adorn the walls and floor in great amounts. A few mummified bodies are strewn across the floor, some of them scorched. It seems this sterile environment has prevented any decomposition from taking place."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RoomEntrance2.NotReallySureHow": "[pg]You're not really sure how old these are. What happened here?"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RunFuncPillar.AllJustWishesOf": "We are all just wishes of greater beings, stardust taken will and form. But as they have Ascended us, we can Ascend ourselves."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RunFuncPillar.ForgetItselfAndLet": "How to forget itself, and let the soul rise forth."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RunFuncPillar.GoneThroughMuchTo": "You have gone through much, to be here. What your body Endures, your soul Learns. And what the soul Learns, it can make material."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RunFuncPillar.LightPureEnergy": "You are light. Pure energy."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RunFuncPillar.OneLessonYourBody": "There is one lesson your body has yet to Endure."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RunFuncPillar.RiseThroughPillar": "Rise through the Pillar. Though your mind cannot comprehend it, your soul Knows it."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.RunFuncPillar.WelcomeWord": "Welcome, [name]."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Staircase.ReachedTheEndOf": "Having reached the end of the width of the pillar, you climb the staircase. More statues rest on the steps, some broken, some intact."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Staircase.RegardlessYouSeemTo": "[pg]Regardless, you seem to be making progress, and haven't fallen into another trap. You spot the end of the stairs ahead. Just in time, you think. Your [legs] are burning from all this climbing."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.Staircase.StepsIncrediblyNumerous": "[pg]The steps are incredibly numerous. You look back and notice that you're a lot higher than what you previously thought possible when you first began climbing; it seems this Tower is once again defying space."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StatueBadEnd.AdventurousLuckyExplorer": "[pg]The adventurous and lucky explorer venturing in the Volcanic Crag could eventually find a massive obsidian tower, lost to time and memory, an ode to the endless power of wizards before the demon plague."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StatueBadEnd.NothingMuchChanges": "Nothing much changes in Mareth, although the Champion's acquaintances always wondered where [he] met his end."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StatueBadEnd.WouldNeedSkill": "[pg]He would have to be skilled if he wanted a chance at exploring its secrets, however; for there was one sentinel keeping a silent watch, a marble guardian eternally protecting its gates, unbidden by the searing heat and the dust storms. Wearing [his] [armor] and wielding [his] [weapon]. Forever."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.AboutTheWholePummeling": "[pg][say: Ah, it's about the whole \"pummeling me into tiny pieces\" thing, right? I got better. No hard feelings. In fact, I feel better than ever! My mind is... clear, for the first time in ages!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.ArchwayOnTheBack": "[pg]An archway on the back of the room leads to another corridor."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.AskJeremiahWhy": "[pg]You ask Jeremiah why he's unwilling to part with his knowledge. He strokes his stone beard."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.BrandishYourAndLook": "[pg]You brandish your [weapon] and look at him menacingly, waiting to see what his reaction will be."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.CirceBows": "[pg]You look at Circe. She bows her head slightly to greet you, her face evidently angered over being called an old lady. [say: Yes, [name], join us. You can take Jeremiah's wine, I'm sure the old man wouldn't mind.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.CirceSighs": "[pg]Circe sighs."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.GetsUpFromChair": "[pg][say: Certainly a possibility. Well, if that's the case...] Circe gets up from her chair, finishing her glass of wine with a long gulp."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.HeSaysChuckling": "[pg][say: Oh, don't I know it!] he says, chuckling. [say: And I tried to kill you twice!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.HeStaresThatIs": "[pg]He stares at you. [say: Hello, [name]. That is your name, right? Nice pose.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.IfTheresOneThing": "[pg][say: Well, if there's one thing that I learned from living here for decades, is that no one should ever trust a solitary sorcerer without drilling into their minds a bit. They quite often go insane, and have powers beyond comprehension! A dangerous combination.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.JeremiahMayHaveAnswers": "[pg]<b>Jeremiah may have better answers for some questions now.</b>"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.JeremiahSmilesToYou": "[pg]Jeremiah smiles to you, and, in a flash, both of them vanish."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.JeremiahTestedMe": "[pg][say: So, Jeremiah here decided to test me on my merits first, and he's just rambling about his past, for the most part. I can tell he's incredibly wise, but his time here has certainly torn holes in his mind.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.LiftsHerHandTowards": "[pg]Circe lifts her hand towards the statue, as if to say [say: See?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.LowerYourWeapon": "[pg]You lower your weapon. He seems honest, after all."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.NarrowEyesAndLook": "[pg]You narrow your eyes and look at his marble face. He seems just as oblivious as before."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.NeitherCirceOrJeremiah": "[pg]Sounds like neither Circe or Jeremiah are solitary wizards anymore."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.OldLadyShowedUp": "[pg][say: Why, hello, [name]. This old lady showed up here just now and started talking to me with several strange and difficult words. You can join in too!]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.PartiallySurprisedToSee": "[pg]You're partially surprised to see Circe sitting on a chair, chatting with Jeremiah over a glass of wine. Two glasses of wine, in fact, although Jeremiah has trouble sipping from his, the goblet itself being further than two feet away from him. He looks at you and smiles in his usual kind but confused manner."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.PeculiarWorkInProgress": "[pg]A peculiar work in progress lies on the other end of the room. It is a massive slab of marble, about 12 feet fall. A bearded, bald old man is half sculpted out of the slab; his upper body has been carved with the same quality as the other statues, but its lower half is just unsculpted marble."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.PointOutForAll": "[pg]You point out that, for all intents and purposes, <i>he</i> is a solitary wizard."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.ReachStudyRoomAgain": "You reach the study room again, and your eyes widen when you look to the end of the room. Jeremiah is there, completely reformed!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.RemainsOfJeremiah": "[pg]The remains of Jeremiah stand at the end of the room."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.SaysClutchingHerFist": "[pg][say: Don't be a stranger, [name],] Circe says, clutching her fist."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.SeemUnfazedByRemark": "[pg]Jeremiah seem unfazed by her remark. [say: The old lady asked for my knowledge on the creation of golems and the Inquisitor's techniques for arcane smithing. Says it's for \"the good of Mareth\", \"the future of magic\", \"to get a new perspective\" and other big-brained bromides. Oh my, she's a wizard alright.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.SomewhereMorePrivate": "[pg][say: We're going to have this discussion somewhere more comfortable.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.SquareOnFloor": "You see a square on the floor on the other end of the room that is particularly lacking in dust and ash. Just the place where Jeremiah used to rest."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.StairsLeadTo": "The stairs lead to what appears to be a study room, of scale proportional to the rest of the tower. Several statue pieces are strewn across the place, and the many bookshelves are destroyed, their books burned to the point of unreadability. The alchemy tables are also destroyed, their fluids dried and stuck to the floor. Various weapons, from swords to spears and riding crops are also on the floor, destroyed."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.StandsAtEnd": "[pg]Jeremiah stands at the end of the room, as he always does."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.TakeGobletAndSit": "[pg]You take the goblet and sit on a large block of marble. You ask them what they're chatting about."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.TalkingAboutWhatever": "[pg][say: We're talking about whatever happens to go through Jeremiah's mind. There's plenty in there that can't be found anywhere else, especially now that Vilkus burned everything to ash. He's... difficult to understand sometimes, though.]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.TellHerThatThats": "[pg]You tell her that that's a certainty, considering what transpired here, but he may also just be testing her patience."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.StudyRoom.WavesHerHandsCreating": "[pg]She waves her hands, creating a circle of pure energy around herself and Jeremiah. You look at him, and he raises and lowers his brow repeatedly, probably interpreting her sentence in a completely different way."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.TheChamber.ChamberVilkusResided": "The chamber Vilkus resided in is now silent, the lethicite crystals turned gray and powerless. Vilkus' ashes have been carried by the winds and spread throughout Mareth; perhaps his intended way of departing life."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.TheChamber.PillarOfLightSits": "[pg]A pillar of light sits at the center of the room, of obvious magical source."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.ToGatePuzzle.FrustratingSearch": "[pg]After several minutes of frustrating search, you spot a small magical circle etched between the lines that separate each door of the gate. Upon placing your hand there for a few seconds, several glowing words appear on the surface of the gate, as if written by an invisible hand carrying a red-hot pen.[pg]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.ToGatePuzzle.ThreeWizardsCongregated": "[say: Three Wizards congregated to built this tower. Althanos, Laurentius, Garland. One of them is the First.][pg][say: Althanos claims he is the First.][pg][say: Laurentius claims Garland is not the First.][pg][say: Garland claims he is not the First.][pg][say: At least one of them is telling the truth. At least one of them is lying. Who is the First?]"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.ToGatePuzzle.TouchSurfaceOfThe": "You touch the surface of the tower once again, attempting to find a way to open the gate."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.UpperCorridor.CorridorInTheTower": "You are in a corridor in the upper levels of the Tower. It is much more narrow than the one that led you to the massive room with the pillar, but it is otherwise similar, made of polished obsidian, adorned with glowing runes. In contrast with the other rooms, it is devoid of signs of battle, statues or corpses."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.UpperCorridor.LittleProgressBeforeFinding": "[pg]You make little progress before finding another thing stopping you. This time, it is a stone door, sealed shut and protected by some kind of energy field. A cursory examination of the gate reveals its sturdiness is too high for anything short of an army of wizards, minotaurs, or both, to have any chance of destroying. You'll have to find a key."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.VictoryAgainstSentinels.DontUnderstandWhatMagic": "[pg]You don't understand what magic enchanted these statues, or why they stand guard here, but you know that the answer must lie inside."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.VictoryAgainstSentinels.HeardSoundOfStone": "[pg]You heard the sound of stone once again, and ready your [weapon] as you turn around. To your surprise, the Warrior is back up, holding his spear with a single hand. He dashes to your direction and fiercely throws his weapon at you!"
  "Scenes.WizardTower.VictoryAgainstSentinels.MoveTowardsGateOnce": "[pg]You move towards the gate once again, moving past the Naked Man, cracked in half, and the Wizard, her remaining hand clutching her stone book tightly. You touch the smooth surface of the gate, looking for some switch to open it."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.VictoryAgainstSentinels.OneDecisiveStrike": "With one decisive strike, the final living statue falls."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.VictoryAgainstSentinels.WeakenedConditionImpaired": "[pg]Fortunately, his weakened condition impaired his aim, and the spear crashes onto the tower, making a small scratch on its surface as the weapon is obliterated into several pieces. The Warrior falls to the ground, shattering, and definitely ending the fight."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.VilkusGameOver.AfterLifeSnuffedOut": "After your life is snuffed out of your body, Vilkus burns your body to ashes with a mighty magical fire."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.VilkusGameOver.GustOfWindEnters": "[pg]A gust of wind enters the chamber through the hole in its ceiling and washes down onto the floor. Your ashes are carried out of the tower, and spread through the land. A warning to any foe that dare cross the long-forgotten Inquisition."
  "Scenes.WizardTower.VilkusGameOver.SitsOnWeatheredThrone": "[pg]Vilkus sits on his weathered throne again, waiting for a revelation that might never come."
}
